{
  "_comment": "Canonical cross-runtime mines:v1 test vectors. Reproducible by any runtime (native Rust, wasm, TS) from the pinned algorithm below. All values are integer/ppm; no floating point. Generated by an independent python3 reference: libs/games/scripts/gen_vectors.py.",
  "algorithm": {
    "game_type": "mines:v1",
    "derivation": "v1",
    "grid": "5x5 = 25 tiles, indices 0..24; mine_count in 1..=24",
    "seed_derivation": "digest(decision, chunk) = blake2b-256 of b'99dot5:engine-seed:v1' (21 bytes, no terminator) || u8 len(game_type) || game_type || u8 len(server_seed) || server_seed || u8 len(client_seed) || client_seed || decision u32 LE || chunk u32 LE. The three text fields are their ASCII bytes as fed to the engine (the 64-hex strings in production) and may not exceed 255 bytes. A decision's randomness is read sequentially from chunk 0, 32 bytes per chunk, at most 4 chunks (128 bytes). preimage_example_hex is the preimage for game_type 'hilo:v1', server_seed '11'*32, client_seed '22'*32, decision 3, chunk 1. mines:v1: the bet is decision 0 and reads 4 stream bytes per mine, sequentially (chunk 0, then chunk 1, ...; 24 mines use 96 bytes). The layout is fixed at bet time; reveals, cashouts and banks draw nothing",
    "preimage_example_hex": "",
    "preimage_example_digest_hex": "e032790ea31b22d5299594aa1de0d461e67cc3b398d5aec5d4685d98684599db",
    "layout": "partial Fisher-Yates over tiles [0..25): draw i consumes 4 stream bytes as a little-endian u32 raw; swap_index = i + ((raw * (25 - i)) >> 32) (Lemire wide-reduction, unbiased); swap tiles[i] <-> tiles[swap_index]. After mine_count draws, mines = sorted(tiles[0..mine_count])",
    "step_multiplier": "revealing the k-th safe tile (k 0-indexed): fair_step_ppm = half_up((25 - k) * 1e6 / (safe - k)) with safe = 25 - mine_count. Every reveal carries the house edge: offered_step_ppm = half_up(fair_step_ppm * 995000 / 1e6) for every k, so round RTP is 0.995^k rather than a flat 0.995",
    "cumulative": "starts at 1e6; each safe reveal multiplies: cum = half_up(cum * offered_step_ppm / 1e6), so cum(k) = 0.995^k * fair(k) and RTP is 99.5% per reveal, compounding to 0.995^k over the round. Revealing a mine sets 0 and settles as a loss. Revealing the last safe tile auto-settles as a win",
    "payout": "the value model is a (banked, live) pair in integer micro-tez: live starts at stake * 1e6 and each safe reveal folds live' = half_up(live * offered_step_ppm / 1e6). The system 'partial-cashout' action (borsh payload: amount u128 LE, in the asset's atomic units) moves amount from live to banked without touching the multiplier chain. Cashout (allowed after >= 1 reveal) and a full clear and the system 'abandon' action pay banked + live (abandon settles abandoned, but at the position's current value, sec-28); a mine hit pays banked (never less: the banked part is already the player's)",
    "action_borsh": "place-bet payload = borsh(Config { mine_count: u32 LE }); reveal payload = borsh(tile_index: u32 LE); cashout payload is empty",
    "house_edge_ppm": 995000,
    "scale_ppm": 1000000,
    "rounding": "half-up (midpoint away from zero), mirroring game-engine-core/src/fixed_point.rs"
  },
